},{"title":"<>","target":"https://github.com/d3/d3-color/blob/master/src/lab.js \"Source\"","line":91},{"title":"0, 360).\n\nIf *l*, *c*, and *h* are specified, these represent the channel values of the returned color; an *opacity* may also be specified. If a CSS Color Module Level 3 *specifier* string is specified, it is parsed and then converted to CIELCh<sub>ab</sub> color space. See [color","target":"#color","line":95},{"title":"CIELCh<sub>ab</sub> color picker","target":"http://bl.ocks.org/mbostock/3e115519a1b495e0bd95","line":95},{"title":"CIELCh<sub>ab</sub>","target":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CIELAB_color_space#Cylindrical_representation:_CIELCh_or_CIEHLC","line":95},{"title":"*color*","target":"#color","line":97},{"title":"*color*.rgb","target":"#color_rgb","line":97},{"title":"<>","target":"https://github.com/d3/d3-color/blob/master/src/cubehelix.js \"Source\"","line":99},{"title":"Cubehelix color picker","target":"http://bl.ocks.org/mbostock/ba8d75e45794c27168b5","line":103},{"title":"Cubehelix","target":"http://www.mrao.cam.ac.uk/~dag/CUBEHELIX/","line":103},{"title":"color","target":"#color","line":105},{"title":"*color*","target":"#color","line":105},{"title":"*color*.rgb","target":"#color_rgb","line":105}],"class_name":"SmartBlock","last_embed":{"hash":"6y1qqe","at":1770841569303}},
